=== A. FQS/Kac unitary minimal models (c < 1) ===
  m=3: c = 1/2    = 0.50000; primaries h = 0, 1/16, 1/2
  m=4: c = 7/10   = 0.70000; primaries h = 0, 3/80, 1/10, 7/16, 3/5, 3/2
  m=5: c = 4/5    = 0.80000; primaries h = 0, 1/40, 1/15, 1/8, 2/5, 21/40, 2/3 ...
  m=6: c = 6/7    = 0.85714; primaries h = 0, 1/56, 1/21, 5/56, 1/7, 3/8, 10/21 ...
  m=7: c = 25/28  = 0.89286; primaries h = 0, 3/224, 1/28, 15/224, 3/28, 5/32, 5/14 ...
  m=8: c = 11/12  = 0.91667; primaries h = 0, 1/96, 1/36, 5/96, 1/12, 35/288, 1/6 ...
  c(m) -> 1 as m -> inf; unitary c < 1 is exactly this discrete set (FQS 1984, GKO coset construction)

