=== D. hostile at c = 1: XXZ, x_1 = L (E_{Sz=1} - E_0) / (2 pi v) vs Bethe ansatz ===
  Bethe: v = pi sqrt(1-D^2) / (2 arccos D);  x_1 = (pi - arccos D) / (2 pi)  [= 1/4 at D = 0]
  Delta=-0.6: x_1(L=12,16,20) = [0.1492 0.1485 0.1482]   Bethe x_1 = 0.1476
  Delta=-0.3: x_1(L=12,16,20) = [0.2031 0.2024 0.2021]   Bethe x_1 = 0.2015
  Delta=+0.0: x_1(L=12,16,20) = [0.2514 0.2508 0.2505]   Bethe x_1 = 0.2500
  Delta=+0.3: x_1(L=12,16,20) = [0.2994 0.299  0.2988]   Bethe x_1 = 0.2985
  Delta=+0.6: x_1(L=12,16,20) = [0.351  0.3514 0.3517]   Bethe x_1 = 0.3524
  Delta=+0.9: x_1(L=12,16,20) = [0.4103 0.4137 0.4159]   Bethe x_1 = 0.4282
  => at c = 1 the exponent is a continuous function of a microscopic coupling: no rigidity
